<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-5172] .NET: Dynamic type registration uses assembly-qualified type name</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5172</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;BinaryProcessor.RegisterType&lt;/tt&gt; uses &lt;tt&gt;AssemblyQualifiedName&lt;/tt&gt;, which includes assembly version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This has two issues:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;We ignore current name mapper, so this type name is not the same as type name in binary metadata, marshaller, etc&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;This breaks when same type comes from assemblies with different versions, which is a valid scenario. Binary protocol is flexible and does not care about type versions, it tolerates new or missing fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
